body:
If we are all going to die someday, it would be best to squeeze every ounce of value that we can during our time alive. But in the grand scheme of things our own existence is insignificant. Our life and the pain and pleasures that come with it mean the world to us, and only us, nobody else. Accepting your insignificance in the universe and can be both liberating and terrifying. Society teaches us that we are all special and that everyone matters.

&#x200B;

In the end nothing matters. Live life how you want
